# Everything here deploys to Linux; text files MUST be LF in the working
# tree. Without this, a host clone with core.autocrlf=true (e.g. a
# ~/.gitconfig carried over from the Windows dev box) checks out CRLF
# and bash dies at line 6 of bootstrap.sh:
#   set: 'pipefail\r': invalid option name
# Attributes beat core.autocrlf, so this pins it on every machine.
# Note: sandbox/Dockerfile COPYs entrypoint.sh + shim/shim.py from the
# host checkout — a CRLF checkout also bakes CRLF scripts into the
# image (bad interpreter on exec), so rebuild after normalizing.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.pyc binary
